  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the minimum probability of any outcome in each lottery and prefers the lottery with the lower minimum probability. This would favor Lottery B (min probability 1%) over A (min probability 100%). However, the individual in the verbal report chooses Lottery A because it is certain and avoids any risk of loss, indicating a preference for certainty and aversion to any nonzero chance of getting nothing. The individual values the absence of any risk, which is inconsistent with the logic of the decision reason, which would favor B for having a smaller minimum probability. The individual considers the 1% probability of loss in B but uses it to argue against B, whereas the decision reason would use the same low probability to favor B. Thus, the information considered (certainty vs. risk) and the justification (preference for safety) contradict the decision reason’s logic. There is no indication that the individual is comparing minimum probabilities in the way the reason defines them. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
